WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.460
Have you ever felt that the summer has passed,

2
00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:04.420
and you never had a summer adventure?

3
00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:06.760
We haven't.

4
00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:08.440
Only in a dream!

5
00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:13.740
Every year at the beginning of August we set up camp in Vlasotince by the river.

6
00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:16.160
Are we far from home? No.

7
00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:18.820
From 2019 up to today

8
00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:21.240
we've missed only one year — 2020.

9
00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:23.500
Then we couldn't because of the virus,

10
00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:27.000
and, like every year, this camp begins with preparation.

11
00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:28.320
Today is July 30.

12
00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:31.620
On today's list we have: buy barrels for the raft,

13
00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:33.360
cut wood for benches and the campfire,

14
00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:36.160
buy a mattress to sleep on and bring my tent from the village.

15
00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:37.840
As for the barrels for the raft,

16
00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:41.060
we were going to drive all the way to Novi Sad, because we found them cheap there.

17
00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:44.140
But just as we were about to give up,

18
00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:46.220
David found them, guess where?

19
00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:48.360
At a dump on his own street.

20
00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:55.690
We're heading home. That is, to the dump.

21
00:00:55.910 --> 00:00:57.410
Wait, let me... Don't, don't.

22
00:01:00.150 --> 00:01:02.730
We bought six, that's enough.

23
00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:04.530
And now we're heading to Stefan:

24
00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:07.010
he offered to cut down his walnut tree for benches.

25
00:01:24.170 --> 00:01:25.850
There it is, that's the one walnut tree, right?

26
00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:27.410
Yes, so that it falls over there.

27
00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:29.490
By two we have to leave for Leskovac.

28
00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:18.150
Good.

29
00:03:18.150 --> 00:03:21.150
The firewood is successfully sawn and ready for the camp.

30
00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:23.030
And now we're heading home to wash up

31
00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:25.730
and heading to Leskovac to buy a mattress to sleep on.

32
00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:33.530
Folks, welcome to Jysk.

33
00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:38.260
Like, I wanted to buy this one.

34
00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:40.280
And this one...

35
00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:43.480
But there's a discount.

36
00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:05.060
I'm a meter and two wild strawberries.

37
00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:06.520
Wide, bro.

38
00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:10.660
And I think it's narrow.

39
00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:13.140
Buddy, I just need to sleep over.

40
00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:15.540
Okay, we're taking this one.

41
00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:19.620
Of course, I had to spend money on more things that I supposedly need.

42
00:04:20.060 --> 00:04:23.980
And the last task before the camp: I have to bring my tent.

43
00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:25.560
We're going to the village of Kruševica.

44
00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:26.940
To the very edge of the village,

45
00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:28.900
where my grandfather's weekend house is.

46
00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:31.380
But since we'd already left the road,

47
00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:33.680
our reckless side won out.

48
00:05:30.070 --> 00:05:30.470
Oops.

49
00:05:39.690 --> 00:05:40.490
David, look.

50
00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:46.980
And on the way back David wanted to ride on the roof too.

51
00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:04.540
Milan, go left, go left.

52
00:06:05.020 --> 00:06:06.200
Even more left.

53
00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:15.020
TV.

54
00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:18.600
Milan, what are you talking about, what TV, damn.

55
00:06:22.540 --> 00:06:24.960
We successfully completed all the tasks on the list.

56
00:06:25.060 --> 00:06:26.940
And then lay down to get some sleep.

57
00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:30.160
July 31, start of the camp.

58
00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:33.540
While I was still asleep, Stefan and David took the firewood to Marička —

59
00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:35.720
the beach where we set up camp every year.

60
00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:38.640
And then David went home to gather his things

61
00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:40.480
and look for anything that might be useful to us.

62
00:06:40.480 --> 00:06:42.220
Let me turn it on, see whether it works.

63
00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:44.080
It doesn't work.

64
00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:51.440
It's plugged in here, let's just see whether the current gets this far.

65
00:06:52.460 --> 00:06:54.200
And, as we see, there's current,

66
00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:57.140
so I don't know why it doesn't work here.

67
00:06:57.840 --> 00:06:59.900
We figured out why it doesn't work: the bulb burned out.

68
00:07:06.290 --> 00:07:09.170
I also came across poles for a pavilion.

69
00:07:09.550 --> 00:07:12.130
I'll take them along anyway, we'll think of something.

70
00:07:12.330 --> 00:07:15.050
In the end David brought his trailer tent

71
00:07:15.050 --> 00:07:16.630
and finally came by for me.

72
00:07:26.060 --> 00:07:28.100
Let the camping season begin.

73
00:07:52.610 --> 00:07:53.650
Welcome to my tent.

74
00:07:53.870 --> 00:07:56.770
As you can see, the tent isn't fully stretched yet,

75
00:07:56.770 --> 00:08:00.270
but now we'll secure it all with these stakes.

76
00:08:00.910 --> 00:08:02.030
What did you do with it, David?

77
00:08:03.090 --> 00:08:04.410
We're going outside to drive in the stakes.

78
00:08:04.490 --> 00:08:05.150
Did you bring a hammer?

79
00:08:05.850 --> 00:08:05.990
No.

80
00:08:06.170 --> 00:08:07.470
Did you bring something to hammer with?

81
00:08:07.610 --> 00:08:08.050
Nothing.

82
00:08:09.750 --> 00:08:10.930
The first thing that came to hand.

83
00:08:10.930 --> 00:08:11.290
Let's go.

84
00:08:18.210 --> 00:08:19.070
Okay, David?

85
00:08:22.070 --> 00:08:24.190
Bro, I'll be sleeping here for the next ten days.

86
00:08:32.370 --> 00:08:35.230
Looks like I won't have a door this year, oh well.

87
00:08:39.130 --> 00:08:39.550
Okay, enough.

88
00:08:42.890 --> 00:08:43.890
Stefan has come over too.

89
00:08:44.110 --> 00:08:46.450
He'll also live with us at the camp for a few days.

90
00:08:47.430 --> 00:08:48.490
Let's throw it in here.

91
00:08:56.320 --> 00:08:57.600
Come on, come here, check into the room.

92
00:08:57.760 --> 00:08:58.620
How do you like the room?

93
00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:05.560
Actually we were supposed to start the camp yesterday.

94
00:09:05.660 --> 00:09:07.280
But some rain came.

95
00:09:07.360 --> 00:09:11.300
We were afraid the weather would turn bad.

96
00:09:11.380 --> 00:09:13.160
But it turned out fine.

97
00:09:13.260 --> 00:09:15.160
It rained last night, now it's dry.

98
00:09:15.580 --> 00:09:17.080
Let the camping begin.

99
00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:19.380
And after we set up my tent,

100
00:09:19.380 --> 00:09:21.420
it was David's trailer's turn.

101
00:09:34.270 --> 00:09:35.130
I got pinched.

102
00:09:37.690 --> 00:09:39.490
And my nearest neighbor David.

103
00:09:40.050 --> 00:09:41.570
Here I am, here's David.

104
00:09:42.170 --> 00:09:45.710
David, the top part where you lie didn't settle into place properly.

105
00:09:46.110 --> 00:09:46.450
There you go.

106
00:09:47.310 --> 00:09:47.610
Like this?

107
00:09:47.610 --> 00:09:49.110
Yes, now it's perfect.

108
00:09:49.390 --> 00:09:50.310
And it's level.

109
00:10:10.910 --> 00:10:14.990
We left Stefan to assemble this vestibule of David's,

110
00:10:14.990 --> 00:10:17.050
because we're in a hurry, it's slowly getting dark.

111
00:10:17.170 --> 00:10:19.810
We need to go see the man up there who gives us electricity,

112
00:10:19.810 --> 00:10:24.070
ask him to give us current this year too, while we're in the camp.

113
00:10:24.190 --> 00:10:25.950
So let's go see what he says.

114
00:10:25.950 --> 00:10:27.470
Yes, we live in the camp with electricity.

115
00:10:27.470 --> 00:10:29.110
We also have to work while we're on the camp.

116
00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:30.590
Good afternoon.

117
00:10:32.890 --> 00:10:36.150
Every year, while we're at the camp, we take electricity from you.

118
00:10:36.370 --> 00:10:42.850
So we want to ask whether we can take electricity from you again.

119
00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:45.730
We offer again: if something needs to be paid,

120
00:10:45.890 --> 00:10:47.230
it's no problem for us.

121
00:10:47.510 --> 00:10:50.330
We haven't set up the camp yet, first we came to ask you

122
00:10:50.530 --> 00:10:51.590
whether we can or not.

123
00:10:52.270 --> 00:10:53.150
Yes, you can.

124
00:10:53.150 --> 00:10:54.550
You all heard.

125
00:10:54.750 --> 00:10:56.650
We're going for cables and David's things.

126
00:10:56.910 --> 00:10:57.890
And also for Milan.

127
00:10:58.350 --> 00:10:59.030
Come on, get ready.

128
00:10:59.250 --> 00:10:59.590
Where to?

129
00:11:00.170 --> 00:11:01.090
Down to the camp.

130
00:11:01.470 --> 00:11:02.910
Hey, projector, projector.

131
00:11:03.410 --> 00:11:04.550
There it is, folks, the projector.

132
00:11:06.370 --> 00:11:08.050
And this is what the trunk looks like

133
00:11:08.390 --> 00:11:09.830
with just David's things.

134
00:11:10.190 --> 00:11:10.970
The guy is moving house.

135
00:11:12.390 --> 00:11:14.470
David stayed to help with something at home,

136
00:11:14.470 --> 00:11:16.450
and Milan and I laid the first cable.

137
00:11:16.670 --> 00:11:19.970
The cable has to go across the meadow, under the dirt road,

138
00:11:19.970 --> 00:11:21.570
and then through the forest to our camp.

139
00:11:27.480 --> 00:11:28.760
We'll have to dig too.

140
00:11:28.860 --> 00:11:29.480
All right, folks.

141
00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:34.080
Now we start digging this trench where we'll lay the cable.

142
00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:36.580
First I have to cut this corrugated hose

143
00:11:36.580 --> 00:11:37.600
so the cable can pass through.

144
00:11:54.750 --> 00:11:55.750
Update, folks.

145
00:11:56.330 --> 00:12:00.810
It got dark, and we're only now finishing digging this trench for the cable.

146
00:12:01.090 --> 00:12:03.490
Now I have to walk through this forest in pitch darkness

147
00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:05.810
to lay the remaining cables.

148
00:12:05.810 --> 00:12:07.630
Here David returned to the camp

149
00:12:07.630 --> 00:12:10.030
and brought us food to regain our strength.

150
00:12:14.150 --> 00:12:14.790
This is mine.

151
00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:18.130
Well, folks, enjoy your meal, let's go eat,

152
00:12:18.130 --> 00:12:20.630
and then we go up into the forest to run the electricity.

153
00:12:20.910 --> 00:12:22.970
See you in a couple of minutes, we're just eating.

154
00:12:23.190 --> 00:12:25.650
He and Milan decided to make their way through the forest,

155
00:12:25.650 --> 00:12:27.730
and I waited up top with the wire.

156
00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:02.780
The cable is successfully laid, I didn't film right away.

157
00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:05.660
We also set up the tent where Stefan will sleep,

158
00:13:05.660 --> 00:13:07.420
and inflated our mattresses.

159
00:13:07.940 --> 00:13:11.320
There, here I'll sleep tonight, inside.

160
00:13:12.060 --> 00:13:12.760
That is, Stefan.

161
00:13:24.060 --> 00:13:25.480
The tent is perfect, I see.

162
00:13:25.840 --> 00:13:28.540
And if you were curious what the person who will sleep here looks like...

163
00:13:29.360 --> 00:13:30.580
The person who will sleep here.

164
00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:50.340
But when we finished everything, something unexpected happened.

165
00:13:50.740 --> 00:13:53.820
We laid everything, time to go to bed,

166
00:13:53.820 --> 00:13:56.600
but right now they're raising the dam.

167
00:13:56.920 --> 00:14:00.980
That is, the lake we swim in, the water we swim in,

168
00:14:00.980 --> 00:14:01.920
won't be here tomorrow.

169
00:14:02.040 --> 00:14:04.220
I hope they lower it again to fill the lake.

170
00:14:04.580 --> 00:14:06.780
Otherwise this camp will be a complete failure,

171
00:14:06.780 --> 00:14:09.460
because where will we put the raft if there's no lake?

172
00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:11.420
But soon hope returned to us.

173
00:14:11.620 --> 00:14:14.640
So, folks, it's now one-twenty.

174
00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:18.900
We've just finished, put up this vestibule,

175
00:14:18.900 --> 00:14:20.340
cleaned up all the mess.

176
00:14:20.600 --> 00:14:23.160
We didn't film, it was something like a small get-together,

177
00:14:23.160 --> 00:14:24.100
but there will be more of that.

178
00:14:24.360 --> 00:14:27.860
By the way, the very moment they raised the dam,

179
00:14:27.920 --> 00:14:30.320
when everything was drained, they lowered it again,

180
00:14:30.320 --> 00:14:31.120
and now the lake is filling up,

181
00:14:31.280 --> 00:14:32.120
so tomorrow we swim.

182
00:14:32.360 --> 00:14:33.080
That's all, see you.

183
00:14:33.080 --> 00:14:35.680
And here is the list of all the tasks for this camp:

184
00:14:35.840 --> 00:14:38.040
tie the rope for jumping,

185
00:14:38.040 --> 00:14:39.560
make a campfire,

186
00:14:39.780 --> 00:14:41.760
make benches by the fire,

187
00:14:41.760 --> 00:14:43.420
hang a screen and set up a projector,

188
00:14:43.640 --> 00:14:45.420
build a big raft,

189
00:14:45.420 --> 00:14:46.680
roast a lamb,

190
00:14:47.020 --> 00:14:49.060
invite someone to play or sing for us,

191
00:14:49.060 --> 00:14:51.900
and for me to spend 24 hours on the raft.

192
00:14:52.220 --> 00:14:54.340
Watch the next camping episode.

193
00:14:54.960 --> 00:14:56.420
I want to get down, buddy.